-- ============================================================================
-- Kelmon Fashion — initial schema
--
-- Firebase Auth issues identity; Supabase Postgres holds the data and enforces
-- access through Row Level Security. A user id is a Firebase UID (a 28-character
-- string), so identity columns are `text` and there is no `auth.users` anywhere.
--
-- This file has two halves:
--
--   1. DDL generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-empty --to-schema`, pasted
--      verbatim. Do not hand-edit it — change prisma/schema.prisma and
--      regenerate, or the schema and the migration silently diverge.
--
--   2. Everything Prisma cannot express: CHECK constraints, partial indexes,
--      functions, triggers, RLS policies and storage buckets. Hand-written, and
--      the reason this migration is worth reading.
--
-- This supersedes the earlier supabase/migrations/0001-0003, which were written
-- before Prisma owned the schema. They are collapsed into this one file because
-- the database was still empty, so there was no history worth preserving.
-- ============================================================================

-- gen_random_uuid() comes from pgcrypto, and the tables below default to it, so
-- this has to run first. Prisma's generated DDL does not include it.
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pgcrypto";

